  "title": "Degenerate colorings of planar graphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A graph $G$ is $k$-degenerate if every subgraph of $G$ has a vertex of degree $\\le k$.\n\nConjecture Every simple planar graph has a 5-coloring so that for $1 \\le k \\le 4$, the union of any $k$ color classes induces a $(k-1)$-degenerate graph.",
